  "rationale": "structural: The text prescribes a public API shape and trait set for `CriterionVersion`. The roots implement each part.\n\n- **Type:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#struct[CriterionVersion]` is a tuple struct with a private `String` field. It derives `Clone`, `Debug`, `PartialEq`, `Eq` and `Serialize`, and uses `#[serde(transparent)]`. This matches the prescribed `pub struct CriterionVersion(/* private fields */)` and the listed trait implementations.\n- **Deserialize:** `impl[CriterionVersion/Deserialize<'de>]` supplies `Deserialize<'de>`. It goes through `from_recorded` and rejects `\"*\"`.\n- **`new`:** `impl[CriterionVersion]/fn[new]` has the signature `new(impl Into<String>) -> Self`. It panics on `\"*\"` by calling `from_recorded(...).expect(...)`.\n- **`from_recorded`:** `fn[from_recorded]` returns `None` for `\"*\"` and `Some` for any other string.\n- **`as_str`:** `fn[as_str]` borrows the stored string.\n- **`is_compatible_with`:** `fn[is_compatible_with]` takes `&self` and `Option<&Self>`. It returns true when the saved version is `None` or equal to `self`.\n\nThe roots are the right ones, and no further root is needed. The comparison policy in `checking_records.version_match` is only cited by the subject, so it needs no implementation edge here.\n\nbehavioral: The reviewed tests cover each observable obligation of `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_version`.\n\n- **`new` panics on `\"*\"`.** `validation_tests.rs#fn[concrete_criterion_version_rejects_the_legacy_marker]` calls `CriterionVersion::new(\"*\")` under `#[should_panic]`. Other strings do not panic. `new(\"v42\")`, `new(\"v*\")` and `new(\"anything\")` are all constructed in `validation_tests.rs#fn[wildcard_versions_still_check_inputs_and_errors]`.\n- **`from_recorded` maps `\"*\"` to `None` and any other string to `Some`.** The `wildcard_versions_still_check_inputs_and_errors` test asserts `from_recorded(\"*\").is_none()`. It also decodes `\"v41\"`, `\"v42\"`, `\"V42\"`, `\"v*\"` and the empty string as `Some`, and the comparison results show they stay distinct. `tests/storage.rs#fn[record_preserves_the_stored_version_encoding]` asserts that `\"review-v1\"` gives `Some` and `\"*\"` gives `None`.\n- **`as_str` borrows the original string.** `record_preserves_the_stored_version_encoding` asserts `as_str()` returns `\"review-v1\"` for a decoded version. No test calls `as_str` on a value built with `new`. That path has no conditional or transformation of its own, so it needs no separate test.\n- **`is_compatible_with`, applying the cited `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.checking_records.version_match`.** The table in `wildcard_versions_still_check_inputs_and_errors` covers each case:\n  - a differing version is rejected (`v41` vs `v42`);\n  - a prefix is rejected (`v42` vs `v420`);\n  - a case difference is rejected (`V42` vs `v42`);\n  - an exact match passes;\n  - a saved `v*` matches only a requested `v*`;\n  - a saved `None` (from `\"*\"`) matches any requested version.\n  \n  The same test also exercises `Record::is_current` with a saved `None`, a mismatched version and a matching version.\n- **Trait implementations.** Serialize and Deserialize are covered. `record_preserves_the_stored_version_encoding` asserts that `\"*\"` is rejected when deserializing a `CriterionVersion` directly. It also asserts that the record wire encoding round-trips unchanged. `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `Clone` and `Debug` are plain trait implementations that carry no behavior of their own to test.\n- **Public signature.** `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the exported inventory against the spec. That is structural, not behavioral.\n\nI found no behavioral gap.",
